2115dae22666c8848086"}, "language": "english", "review": "The mil-sim to end all mil-sims. While there is a single player, you really need to come into this game wanting to find mods and a community of people to play with. It's a sandbox of tools that is highly focused on simulating contemporary combat. You need to come into this game wanting that experience of hiking 20 minutes to find any combat - and it could end without you firing a shot after all that. \n\nPerformance wise, this game runs okay now, especially as computers have gotten more powerful. There are a lot of background processes and scripts so it's more CPU intensive than a typical shooter. Speaking of shooting, it's not very satisfying and intentionally feels clunky. Team work, positioning, and tactics are vastly more important that your ability to click on heads.", "timestamp_created": 1755279814, "timestamp_updated": 1755279814, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.512124717235565186", "comment_count": 0, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}]}